  "source_reconstruction": {
    "cadence": "The checkpoint layer_types are ten exact repetitions of five sliding_attention layers followed by one full_attention layer.",
    "consumer": "TritonAttnBackend.forward_decode selects window_kv_indptr/indices for local layers and full kv_indptr/indices for global layers, then passes the layer-specific K/V buffers to decode_attention_fwd. Target verification uses extend_attention_fwd.",
    "native_reuse": "On Hopper and local head dimension 256, extend_attention uses BLOCK_M=64 and BLOCK_N=64. The 12 NGRAM queries fit one M tile, so a CTA streams prefix K/V once for all queries. Two query heads share each KV head; their whole-batch reuse footprint is below even the 30 MiB contention scenario.",
    "native_reuse_uncertainty": "The fit is source-and-address-model evidence, not a measured H100 hit rate. CUDA block execution order is not a semantic guarantee; scope-matched DRAM/L2 counters that show paired-head eviction would invalidate this typed none.",
    "ownership": "req_pool_indices select request rows; req_to_token[row, logical position] owns page-size-one token locations. The backend gathers the last min(seq_len, 1023) locations and, for SWAKVPool, translates full locations to SWA locations before the layer buffer consumer.",
    "processed_head_geometry": "Gemma raw base fields describe local attention (16 KV heads, head dimension 256); SGLang preserves them as swa_* and maps global_* to the full path (4 KV heads, head dimension 512).",
    "producer": "Gemma4Attention forwards layer-specific K/V with save_kv_cache; TritonAttnBackend._set_kv_buffer writes through KVWriteLoc to the layer buffer. No KV sharing is configured.",
